<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:21:43Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>As COP31 Antalya kicks off, can world move beyond big promises?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:519430a953716ed979bfb04046be32b07488259232d14f75bb474a5a819d48f5</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:21:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T05:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-cop31-antalya-kicks-off-can-world-move-beyond-big-promises/a-79661366--3ff0bee69cef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-cop31-antalya-kicks-off-can-world-move-beyond-big-promises/a-79661366?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Droughts, floods and extreme heat are upping the pressure on delegates at the UN climate talks in Antalya, Turkey. Can countries move beyond pledges to concrete action?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Poland: Gunman kills 6 in Krakow main square</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:476b1e1d0eddf3f3d0f02ee39f4ab2f4fc0958f47b12c2ebac023b08a8be6f88</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:21:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T21:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-gunman-kills-6-in-krakow-main-square/a-79886489--2e26ae8c4338.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-gunman-kills-6-in-krakow-main-square/a-79886489?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A gunman who fired from a car killed at least six people, including a British tourist, in Krakow's main market square. Officials said the shooter was fascinated with "radical" and "far-right" ideologies.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ebola: Why is there still no vaccine?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59476f09b8aa478ba7519bcf4f5dea5f6037071fadb3c826521bb99cf4b42f0c</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:21:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T21:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ebola-why-is-there-still-no-vaccine/a-79888134--134cc892a91f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ebola-why-is-there-still-no-vaccine/a-79888134?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ebola has been known about for decades, but there is still no vaccine against the Bundibugyo strain of the virus causing the current outbreak. New research raises hopes of protection against the various types of Ebola.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli president tasks Gadi Eisenkot with forming government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59ee9196c37c69bed1627aa8bfb5d97f2e479b28683ec11989c3c25b2c9a880d</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:21:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T19:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israeli-president-tasks-gadi-eisenkot-with-forming-government/a-79888288--1dfc2b75eb80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-president-tasks-gadi-eisenkot-with-forming-government/a-79888288?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Isaac Herzog has picked former Israeli military chief Gadi Eisenkot, leader of an anti-Netanyahu alliance, to take the first shot at trying to form a government, with tricky coalition talks expected.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump offers White House press secretary role to Dana White</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7eb5fe07e9a4f810e1e1ed7512cd584e0d15a93f05d999ab460d5c9fc6ff9e11</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T19:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-offers-white-house-press-secretary-role-to-dana-white/a-79888119--34dff2f985d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-offers-white-house-press-secretary-role-to-dana-white/a-79888119?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump has offered the White House press secretary job to Dana White, the chief executive of the Ultimate Fighting Championship. White has neither formally accepted nor turned down the invitation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France sees new round of Yellow Vest, student protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46e4d8e50bf4b518883cc64b3587d4698906832113e5efc9fa4c1b654a05e162</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T19:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-sees-new-round-of-yellow-vest-student-protests/a-79884064--3a9e4c3fcc71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-sees-new-round-of-yellow-vest-student-protests/a-79884064?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Although fewer protesters turned out in comparison with previous weeks, several cities saw clashes between police and demonstrators.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Armenia's selective prosecution: A threat to EU relations?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad3f60ef4cac2794a565b08e46884c79cc5fde01c99806741ce50d6865a0b379</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/armenia-s-selective-prosecution-a-threat-to-eu-relations/a-79878159--345ae9a3ae32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/armenia-s-selective-prosecution-a-threat-to-eu-relations/a-79878159?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While Brussels has refrained from harsh criticism, Armenian civil society has warned of selective justice against opposition figures. Could the EU's pragmatic stance risk repeating past mistakes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa's ANC facing worst-ever performance in local elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf4bf1c5a15f3e9cf19c4f0d02fc651144a46d5e8c004e89dc36258b4aaf2ea4</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T18:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-s-anc-facing-worst-ever-performance-in-local-elections/a-79887482--0f01de17e4d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-s-anc-facing-worst-ever-performance-in-local-elections/a-79887482?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Near-final results show South Africa's once dominant ANC will see its lowest-ever vote percentage. The party is taking the blame for shoddy municipal services, including water and electricity shortages.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>More than 40,000 gather as Pope Leo XIV celebrates Mass in Uruguay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1c15dc8f68bdba93091444c1e4e3abc6618e6f158451813cb0229c6ca99791f</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/more-than-40-000-gather-as-pope-leo-xiv-celebrates-mass-in-uruguay/a-79886543--b939280d1b50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/more-than-40-000-gather-as-pope-leo-xiv-celebrates-mass-in-uruguay/a-79886543?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Leo celebrated the first Mass of his South America tour less than a month after undergoing cancer surgery. He is seeking to raise interest in the Catholic Church in Uruguay, South America's most secular country.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Journalism and AI: Who owns the news?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5e7a71384bf27f9872f088b36b5d0a1de289f577ca9cc80e67e6e6ad3abf6b7</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T15:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/journalism-and-ai-who-owns-the-news/a-79884854--eca12d826319.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/journalism-and-ai-who-owns-the-news/a-79884854?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Publishers say AI chatbots are using their reporting to answer readers' questions while sending back less traffic and less money. Should the companies that build these tools pay for the journalism they rely on?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Son of Iran's shah receives 'Freedom Prize' in Frankfurt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fdd49af2083552953c8082fccca992d8646cf04dd39910e4fe6be2e349bd5de7</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T14:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/son-of-iran-s-shah-receives-freedom-prize-in-frankfurt/a-79885661--aa99dccac573.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/son-of-iran-s-shah-receives-freedom-prize-in-frankfurt/a-79885661?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">18,000 people gathered in Frankfurt to show support for Reza Pahlavi, the son of the Iranian monarch ousted in 1979. Factions in the opposition have accused him of not distancing himself from his father's rule.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>After victory in the midterms, what next for US Democrats?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2209502b338156d5176d57bb627a78ff0031d7f758f083d839b52af50012fe1c</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T14:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-victory-in-the-midterms-what-next-for-us-democrats/a-79884957--f8ad14f3dbbf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-victory-in-the-midterms-what-next-for-us-democrats/a-79884957?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's Republican party has lost its majority in both chambers of the US Congress. But the president still has a lot of power — and the Democrats have yet to agree on how best to use theirs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy's Meloni blames pro-Russian hackers for cyberattack on minister</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfd7d1bbf9d652acfe23475163e79ba6c235380fdb2c7f1ab6e3f92f9d66c89e</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T14:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-s-meloni-blames-pro-russian-hackers-for-cyberattack-on-minister/a-79885200--f6543501c58b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-s-meloni-blames-pro-russian-hackers-for-cyberattack-on-minister/a-79885200?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Antonio Tajani has said hackers published personal data stolen from him as Giorgia Meloni blamed pro-Russia criminals for the incident. The news follows a string of bomb threats that have grounded flights across the EU.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: 33 killed in strike near Sanaa, Houthis say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ca298b29b768114e1399d83a1a7e41fea7bc9a67149bffb4ac2639705806c50</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:21:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T13:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-33-killed-in-strike-near-sanaa-houthis-say/a-79885177--3e92638e1447.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-33-killed-in-strike-near-sanaa-houthis-say/a-79885177?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Iran-backed Houthi rebel group accused Saudi Arabia of hitting several homes in the village of al-Shariya near the Yemeni capital. There was no initial comment from Riyadh.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>New Zealand election too close to call with over 95% of votes counted</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6769782f360060f1ead66a2f7e30ade8cf79cfc68519de9422e1bae582e35830</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T11:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-zealand-election-too-close-to-call-with-over-95-of-votes-counted/a-79883056--e9f880c38325.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-zealand-election-too-close-to-call-with-over-95-of-votes-counted/a-79883056?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Initial results in New Zealand show the two main parties neck-and-neck with fewer than 4,000 votes separating them. Official results aren't expected until later this month once special votes have been counted.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany hopes to host world ice hockey championship — without Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e81b4f8057841b955832f1d576b2c5223edfea6a6f120074677f83f459c57f5</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-hopes-to-host-world-ice-hockey-championship-without-russia/a-79879536--60661c53ebb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-hopes-to-host-world-ice-hockey-championship-without-russia/a-79879536?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">International protests continue after a court ruled that Russia must be allowed to return to international ice hockey. Germany is seeking a solution that will allow the country to host next year's world championship.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Russia hits Kyiv with airstrikes ahead of trilateral talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c18edd253b38aaf9f787d12ba49cfba5bb03512e553d6040e3094963e2ad70e9</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-hits-kyiv-with-airstrikes-ahead-of-trilateral-talks/a-79883851--55817e315a75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-hits-kyiv-with-airstrikes-ahead-of-trilateral-talks/a-79883851?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The strikes hit a major bridge and energy facilities in the Kyiv region. President Volodymyr Zelenskyy accused Moscow of trying to "push" Ukraine "into a blackout" ahead of talks in Abu Dhabi.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Son of Iran's last shah takes center stage in Frankfurt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7cee3484d29cceb84b6903bd9b1a1592759e64570c86eba4a4c48fbc3e62a4ad</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-son-of-iran-s-last-shah-takes-center-stage-in-frankfurt/live-79883533--726c458ec8d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-son-of-iran-s-last-shah-takes-center-stage-in-frankfurt/live-79883533?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian opposition leader Reza Pahlavi accepted a peace prize in the name of the Iranian people in Frankfurt. Meanwhile, Germany's defense minister said he believes military conscription will not be needed. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Amid protests, France's rising debt costs threaten stability</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c259f5c523433eb39f8531fe5703f947192493678b76d544b79d7959b854583</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amid-protests-france-s-rising-debt-costs-threaten-stability/a-79865654--50648477f294.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amid-protests-france-s-rising-debt-costs-threaten-stability/a-79865654?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France plans to spend an extra €4 billion on education amid nationwide protests. But with public debt mounting and interest costs climbing, how much fiscal room does the government have?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>US: Giant pandas from China make public debut at Atlanta zoo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f89560174a7ce83d05b9fa7b7b1105740a014adaee9c6fab932bb39c24d692f9</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T07:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-giant-pandas-from-china-make-public-debut-at-atlanta-zoo/a-79883388--b468c87ae7ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-giant-pandas-from-china-make-public-debut-at-atlanta-zoo/a-79883388?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ping Ping and Fu Shuang are the first giant pandas to be housed in Zoo Atlanta after a gap of two years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Vehicles major cause of Delhi pollution, top court says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb65fc8d976252317a0142962924074d7df84f2a616576c9d0f173e0d826ea74</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T07:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-vehicles-major-cause-of-delhi-pollution-top-court-says/live-79883248--8418b6668d5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-vehicles-major-cause-of-delhi-pollution-top-court-says/live-79883248?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Supreme Court implored responsible Diwali celebrations as the Indian government sets out to tackle the country's severe air pollution crisis. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
